    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Location words: 桌子上, 房间里",
      "body": "To say where something is, put the thing first, then the location word right after it. 桌子上 means 'on the table' (literally 'table-on'), which is the opposite order from English. Use 在 before the place to say where something is: 书在桌子上. You can also start with the place and use 有 to say what is there: 桌子上有一个杯子. Soon you'll meet 里 (inside), as in 房间里, 'in the room'.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "书在桌子上。",
          "en": "The book is on the table."
        },
        {
          "zh": "桌子上有一个杯子。",
          "en": "There is a cup on the table."
        },
        {
          "zh": "我的手机在桌子上。",
          "en": "My phone is on the table."
        }
